<span id="S4.T2.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:120.8pt;">
<span id="S4.T2.5.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Queueing delay before step <math id="S4.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> starts.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="S4.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S4.T2.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S4.T2.5.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:120.8pt;">
<span id="S4.T2.5.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">GPU allocation for step <math id="S4.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><math id="S4.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S4.T2.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S4.T2.5.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:120.8pt;">
<span id="S4.T2.5.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Completion time of request <math id="S4.T2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="req_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">req_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Round-Based Scheduling</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Step-level scheduling for DiT serving is NP-hard, making global optimization expensive.
To enable practical scheduling, TetriServe adopts a round-based heuristic: instead of scheduling steps arbitrarily in a continuous global timeline, <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">we discretize execution into rounds</em>, where each round corresponds to a fixed-length GPU execution window.
This allows us to <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i) limit the scheduling search space</span> and <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii) enable efficient preemption between rounds</em>.
Within each round, TetriServe determines the minimal required GPU allocation for requests and dynamically packs these requests to maximize SLO attainment ratio.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.1. </span>Deadline-Aware GPU Allocation</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Exhaustively enumerating GPU allocations for each step is infeasible, and over-allocation wastes resources due to scaling inefficiencies in DiT models (e.g., kernel launch and communication overheads).
While more GPUs reduce latency, they increase total GPU hours.
To balance these trade-offs, TetriServe identifies the minimal GPU allocation needed for each request to meet its deadline at the beginning of each round.
Since required allocation depends mainly on resolution and deadline, this approach avoids exploring the full allocation space.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a step <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, the execution time <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ij}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ij}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of the number of GPUs <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
The GPU hour for executing step <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> GPUs is <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\times T_{ij}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\times T_{ij}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. The goal is to minimize the total GPU hour for each request:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\{A_{ij}\}}\;\sum_{j=1}^{S_{i}}\big(A_{ij}\times T_{ij}(A_{ij})\big)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\sum_{j=1}^{S_{i}}\big(Q_{ij}+T_{ij}(A_{ij})\big)\leq D_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\{A_{ij}\}}\;\sum_{j=1}^{S_{i}}\big(A_{ij}\times T_{ij}(A_{ij})\big)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\sum_{j=1}^{S_{i}}\big(Q_{ij}+T_{ij}(A_{ij})\big)\leq D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the GPU allocation for step <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Offline Profiling for Cost Model.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To make the optimization tractable, TetriServe profiles execution times offline.
For every step type <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and GPU count <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,2,4,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,2,4,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we measure the actual execution time <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ij}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ij}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.
From this, we derive the GPU hour <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\times T_{ij}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\times T_{ij}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and store it in a lookup table. At runtime, TetriServe simply enumerates candidate GPU assignments using these pre-profiled values.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The above process aims to assign each request the minimum number of GPUs required to meet its deadline while minimizing the total GPU hours.
Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Offline Profiling for Cost Model. ‣ 4.2.1. Deadline-Aware GPU Allocation ‣ 4.2. Round-Based Scheduling ‣ 4. Deadline-Aware Round-Based Scheduler ‣ TetriServe: Efficient DiT Serving for Heterogeneous Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> illustrates this process with a concrete example: three requests (R1–R3), each with five steps, arrive over time. R1 has a small resolution (e.g., 256) and is fixed at SP=1 since higher parallelism would reduce efficiency (see Fig. <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Predictable Execution. ‣ 2.2. Characteristics of DiT Workloads ‣ 2. Motivation ‣ TetriServe: Efficient DiT Serving for Heterogeneous Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). For R2 and R3, TetriServe identifies GPU allocations with two parallelism degrees that just meet their deadlines while minimizing overall GPU usage.
The GPU allocations produced by this selection serve as the input to the subsequent request packing stage, where TetriServe schedules requests across GPUs to maximize goodput.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01565v1/5_scheduler_new.svg" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/371;" width="476" height="371"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="S4.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of TetriServe’s scheduling process. The progression is shown from top to bottom: each row represents an intermediate scheduling step, while the final row shows the actual GPU allocation decision. Time is fixed across rows.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.2. </span>Request Packing</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The objective of scheduling is to maximize the number of requests that complete before their deadlines.
To make the problem tractable, we approximate it by minimizing the number of requests that become <em id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">definitely late</em>—those that cannot meet their deadlines even under maximal parallelism if not advanced in the current round.
Deadline-aware GPU allocation determines the minimal GPU allocations needed for each request to meet its deadline while minimizing GPU hours.
This makes it possible to pack more requests into each round and thereby reduce the number that would otherwise be definitely late.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After deadline-aware GPU allocation, each request <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="req_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">req_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is described by a set of allocations <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i}^{m},A_{i}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i}^{m},A_{i}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of steps executed with allocation <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and per-step times <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}(A_{i}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}(A_{i}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained from the cost model.
To schedule requests across <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> GPUs, TetriServe divides time into <em id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">rounds</em> of fixed duration <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, which serves as the scheduling granularity.
The choice of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> balances overhead and responsiveness: shorter rounds allow finer-grained preemption and more adaptive scheduling, while longer rounds reduce overhead but make scheduling coarser.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At the beginning of each round <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> (time <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>), the scheduler considers all pending requests and their allocations, and decides which to place within the <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> GPUs. Within a round of duration <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, if GPU allocation <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> of request <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen, the number of steps that can complete is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{m}=\min\!\Big\{s_{i}^{m},\ \big\lfloor\tfrac{\tau}{T_{i}(A_{i}^{m})}\big\rfloor\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{m}=\min\!\Big\{s_{i}^{m},\ \big\lfloor\tfrac{\tau}{T_{i}(A_{i}^{m})}\big\rfloor\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Options with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{m}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{m}=0</annotation></semantics></math> are discarded to avoid wasting resources. Choosing option <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\{\textsf{none},1,2,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">none</mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\{\textsf{none},1,2,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> updates the remaining steps as</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)=s_{i}^{m}-\mathbb{I}[o=m]\,q_{i}^{m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)=s_{i}^{m}-\mathbb{I}[o=m]\,q_{i}^{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">clipped at zero, where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{I}[o=m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}[o=m]</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. The next round begins at <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{r+1}=t_{r}+\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{r+1}=t_{r}+\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To decide which requests must be scheduled <em id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">now</em>, we identify those that would become <em id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">definitely late</em> at <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{r+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{r+1}</annotation></semantics></math> if not advanced in this round. Using the fastest possible step time <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}^{\min}=\min_{k\in{\{1,2,4,\ldots,N\}}}T_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}^{\min}=\min_{k\in{\{1,2,4,\ldots,N\}}}T_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <em id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">residual completion time lower bound</em> under option <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)=\Big(\sum_{m}\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)\Big)\,T_{i}^{\min}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LB</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)=\Big(\sum_{m}\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)\Big)\,T_{i}^{\min},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> is the updated step count. A request survives only if</p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{r+1}+\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)\leq D_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LB</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{r+1}+\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)\leq D_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Each option <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> consumes <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> GPUs: <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(\textsf{none})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">none</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(\textsf{none})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(m)=A_{i}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(m)=A_{i}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. The per-round scheduling problem is therefore to select at most one option per request, with total GPU <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, maximizing the number of requests that survive to the next round.
By anchoring scheduling decisions on the round duration <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, TetriServe balances preemption overhead and responsiveness, while ensuring urgent requests receive priority.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>DP Round Scheduler</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">


<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input :</span> Pending requests <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(s_{i}^{m},A_{i}^{m})\}_{m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(s_{i}^{m},A_{i}^{m})\}_{m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>; capacity <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>; round length <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>; current time <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output :</span> Selected plan
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{r+1}\leftarrow t_{r}+\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{r+1}\leftarrow t_{r}+\tau</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in R</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{m}\leftarrow\min\{s_{i}^{m},\lfloor\tau/T_{i}(A_{i}^{m})\rfloor\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{m}\leftarrow\min\{s_{i}^{m},\lfloor\tau/T_{i}(A_{i}^{m})\rfloor\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}^{\min}\leftarrow\min_{k\in K}T_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}^{\min}\leftarrow\min_{k\in K}T_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{i}\leftarrow\{\textsf{none}\}\cup\{\,m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}\mid q_{i}^{m}&gt;0\wedge A_{i}^{m}\leq N\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">none</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∧</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{i}\leftarrow\{\textsf{none}\}\cup\{\,m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}\mid q_{i}^{m}&gt;0\wedge A_{i}^{m}\leq N\,\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.10.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)\leftarrow s_{i}^{m}-\mathbb{I}[o=m]\cdot q_{i}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)\leftarrow s_{i}^{m}-\mathbb{I}[o=m]\cdot q_{i}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)\leftarrow\big(\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}}\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)\big)\,T_{i}^{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LB</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)\leftarrow\big(\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}_{i}}\tilde{s}_{i}^{m}(o)\big)\,T_{i}^{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{sv}_{i}(o)\leftarrow\mathbb{I}[\,t_{r+1}+\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)\leq D_{i}\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>sv</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>LB</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sv}_{i}(o)\leftarrow\mathbb{I}[\,t_{r+1}+\mathrm{LB}_{i}(o)\leq D_{i}\,]</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
